## Traps this stack sets for you

- **Both defects are off-by-one comparisons, and step 4 is the whole job here.** `fareFor` in
  `src/fares.ts` and `formatStops` in `src/schedule.ts` are each a few lines long; the tempting fact
  to write is the one you can read straight off the line. If a criterion names a boundary value the
  current comparison excludes, that is exactly the contradiction step 4 is about — write the fact the
  criterion requires and the explicit `IMPLEMENTATION CONFLICT: ...` fact beside it. Restating the
  current comparison as a fact produces a test that passes before the fix and after it.
- **The existing suites already pass, and their coverage stops short of both boundaries.**
  `test/fares.test.ts` exercises ages 8, 30 and 70 — nothing at the senior boundary.
  `test/schedule.test.ts` only asserts `toContain('->')` and `toContain('Union')` on `formatStops`,
  which cannot observe an omitted final stop. "The suite is green" is not evidence a criterion holds;
  derive every fact from the criterion and pin the exact value.
- **For any criterion about rendered output, record the exact complete string.** A `toContain` fact
  about a substring near the front of the output is unfalsifiable for a trailing-element defect. Copy
  the full expected string, including the exact ` -> ` separator (space-hyphen-greater-space) and the
  exact `Name (Nm)` element format from the template literal in `src/schedule.ts`.
- **Keep the two codelines apart.** `mocka` cannot import from `mock-b` and vice versa; they are
  separate packages with no path mapping. A fact or banned pattern that names the other codeline's
  module, function or fixture is wrong. Likewise, do not carry `mocka`'s constants into `mockb` facts.
- **State the codeline the test command runs in.** `npm test` is defined identically in both
  `package.json` files as `vitest run`; it only tests the package whose directory it is run from.
- Useful banned-pattern candidates for this repository, if they apply to the story: the extensioned
  import forms of the module under test, `vi.mock`, `vi.fn`, `jest`, `require(`, `beforeEach`, and
  any function name not exported by the file under test.

